 ## Overview
-The Sobel Operator is a gradient estimation method used in volume rendering to compute the spatial gradient vector for each voxel in a scalar volume [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of determining the rate of change of data values to generate opacity functions and shading normals, emphasizing regions of high spatial frequency corresponding to edges [S1]. Unlike general edge detection where spatial location is critical, in volume rendering opacity functions are applied uniformly regardless of position, so the goal is to locate boundaries in the data value domain rather than the spatial domain [S1]. It is distinguished from its sibling [Gradient-based Diffuse Lighting with Alpha Blending](1257-gradient-based-diffuse-lighting-with-alpha-blending.md) by being a fundamental gradient computation primitive rather than a lighting model, and from [Gradient Computation via Finite Differences](1077-gradient-computation-via-finite-differences.md) by using separable smoothing weights that make it less sensitive to noise than simple central differences [S1].
