 ## Background
-The Sobel operator was introduced by Irwin Sobel [S1]. It is an efficient edge detecting operator used for gradient measurement in volume rendering, specifically for opacity function generation and shading [S1]. It is a 2-D spatial gradient measurement operator that emphasizes regions of high spatial frequency corresponding to edges [S1]. In the context of volume rendering, it is used to locate boundaries in the data value domain rather than the spatial domain, as opacity functions are applied uniformly [S1]. It is one of several edge detection kernels, alongside Prewitt, Kirsch, and Robinson, which calculate the 1st derivative [S1].
